// Test: bugfixes/plugin_output_page_boundary
// Regression: COMPILER-PLUGIN-OUTPUT-NULL-BYTE-CORRUPTION-AT-PAGE-BOUNDARY
// (fingerprint 835d361c9515 / cdb735a9453a)
//
// Grammar: grammar.ebnf `plugins_block`, `expand_block_usage`
// Semantic: SEM-PLUGIN-001 (plugin host bridge string integrity)
//
// The reporter observed that plugin output crossing the ~64 KiB WASM page
// boundary surfaced as null bytes, causing tokenizer failures with
// "Invalid indentation at <plugin-output>:N:1".
//
// Root-cause audit on 0.30.388 found NO u16/i16 narrowing casts in any of
// the four core string-passing helpers (read_clean_string, read_raw_string,
// read_lp_from_data, write_clean_string) — all use u32/usize with bounds
// checks. The Rust-level integration test (test_plugin_large_output.rs)
// drives the full production path with a 224 KB (3500×64-byte) deterministic
// payload that crosses three WASM linear-memory pages.
//
// This .cln file documents the pattern at the source level and serves as an
// anchor for the cross-reference: the actual byte-level assertion lives in
// tests/test_plugin_large_output.rs, which compiles the plugin source at
// tests/cln/plugins/large_output_round_trip/main.cln and verifies the
// host receives all bytes intact.
//
// If this test runs through the compiler without tokenizer errors, the
// compiler's plugin host bridge handles large (>64 KB) plugin outputs
// correctly for the clean source side. The Rust integration test verifies
// the byte-level integrity for the host bridge side.
//
// Expected output:
//   page_boundary_ok
//
// Note: this file does NOT load the large_output_round_trip plugin; it only
// verifies the compiler itself compiles this annotation correctly. The actual
// page-boundary regression test is test_plugin_large_output.rs.

start:
	printl("page_boundary_ok")
